@attribute [Route(pageUrl)]
@layout DemosMainLayout

<DemosPageHeadSection PageUrl="@pageUrl"
                      PageTitle="@pageTitle"
                      PageDescription="@pageDescription"
                      MetaTitle="@metaTitle"
                      MetaDescription="@metaDescription"
                      ImageUrl="@imageUrl" />

<div class="mb-3">
    Each example below starts from a problem people hit when they put charts into real business screens, reported in the
    <a href="https://github.com/vikramlearning/blazorbootstrap/issues?q=is%3Aissue%20chart" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Blazor Bootstrap issues</a>
    or common to Chart.js reports. For each chart type and option on its own, see the
    <a href="https://chartjs.blazorexpress.com/demos/samples" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">BlazorExpress.ChartJS samples</a>.
</div>

<Section Size="HeadingSize.H2" Name="Charts that shrink and grow in Bootstrap rows and cards" PageUrl="@pageUrl" Link="responsive-layout">
    <div class="mb-3">
        <strong>The problem:</strong> a chart in a Bootstrap column or a flex card gets smaller when the window narrows but does not grow back, or
        pushes past the edge of its card when a side panel opens
        (<a href="https://github.com/vikramlearning/blazorbootstrap/issues/1089" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">#1089</a>,
        <a href="https://github.com/vikramlearning/blazorbootstrap/issues/797" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">#797</a>).
        Two things cause it. A Bootstrap <code>.col</code> is a flex item, and a flex item never gets narrower than its content, so the canvas holds the column open.
        And Chart.js never makes a chart taller than its container already is; a container without its own height is only as tall as the canvas,
        so the chart can shrink but never grow back.
        <br />
        <strong>The fix:</strong>
        <ol class="mt-2 mb-0">
            <li>Add <code>style="min-width: 0;"</code> to the column or flex item that holds the chart.</li>
            <li>
                Give the chart's container a height that follows its width: <code>ContainerStyle="position: relative; width: 100%; aspect-ratio: 2 / 1; min-height: 240px;"</code>.
                Keep <code>width: 100%</code>; without it, <code>aspect-ratio</code> turns the minimum height into a minimum width and the chart overflows on small screens.
            </li>
            <li>Set <code>MaintainAspectRatio = false</code> in the chart options, so the chart fills that container.</li>
            <li>Do not set <code>Width</code> or <code>Height</code> on the chart; a fixed size stops it following the layout.</li>
        </ol>
    </div>
    <Demo Type="typeof(ChartScenarios_Demo_01_Responsive_Layout)" Tabs="true" />
</Section>

<Section Size="HeadingSize.H2" Name="Days missing from the query result" PageUrl="@pageUrl" Link="missing-dates">
    <div class="mb-3">
        <strong>The problem:</strong> a <code>GROUP BY</code> date query returns only the days that had data, so a chart of orders per day silently
        skips closed days and outages, and the bars look evenly spaced when they are not
        (<a href="https://github.com/vikramlearning/blazorbootstrap/issues/643" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">#643</a>).
        <br />
        <strong>The fix:</strong> build the full list of days for the range in C# and fill the days the query did not return.
        Use <code>0</code> when a missing day means nothing happened, and <code>null</code> when it means no data was reported, so the chart shows a gap.
    </div>
    <Demo Type="typeof(ChartScenarios_Demo_02_Missing_Dates)" Tabs="true" />
</Section>

<Section Size="HeadingSize.H2" Name="Too many slices: top N plus Other" PageUrl="@pageUrl" Link="top-n-other">
    <div class="mb-3">
        <strong>The problem:</strong> a pie or doughnut chart of every customer, country or product turns into thin slices nobody can read,
        and once there are more slices than palette colours, colours repeat.
        <br />
        <strong>The fix:</strong> sort the rows, keep the largest few as their own slices, add the rest together as one <b>Other</b> slice in a neutral colour,
        and list what <b>Other</b> contains next to the chart.
    </div>
    <Demo Type="typeof(ChartScenarios_Demo_03_Top_N_Other)" Tabs="true" />
</Section>

<Section Size="HeadingSize.H2" Name="Keep each category's colour when the data changes" PageUrl="@pageUrl" Link="stable-colors">
    <div class="mb-3">
        <strong>The problem:</strong> colours given by list position move to another category when the data is sorted differently or a category
        has no rows, so <b>Billing</b> is teal in one quarter and orange in the next, and readers compare the wrong slices
        (<a href="https://github.com/vikramlearning/blazorbootstrap/issues/411" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">#411</a>).
        <br />
        <strong>The fix:</strong> give every category a colour once, from the full category list, and look the colour up by name each time you build the data.
        Use the same lookup for every chart on the page.
    </div>
    <Demo Type="typeof(ChartScenarios_Demo_04_Stable_Colors)" Tabs="true" />
</Section>

<ChartJSCallout />

@code {
    private const string pageUrl = DemoRouteConstants.Demos_URL_ChartScenarios;
    private const string pageTitle = "Blazor Chart Scenarios";
    private const string pageDescription = "Fixes for problems people hit when they put charts into real business screens: charts that do not grow back in Bootstrap layouts, days missing from query results, pie charts with too many slices, and colours that move between categories.";
    private const string metaTitle = "Blazor chart scenarios and fixes";
    private const string metaDescription = "Live Blazor chart examples with source code that fix common chart problems: responsive charts in Bootstrap rows and cards, missing dates, top N plus Other, and stable category colours.";
    private const string imageUrl = "https://i.imgur.com/IX3bajc.png";
}
